# Component Rules

## Structure
- One component per file, named `ComponentName.tsx`.
- Co-locate `ComponentName.css.ts` (vanilla-extract) and `ComponentName.stories.tsx`.
- ≤150 lines; split if larger. Named exports only — no `export default`.

## Props & types
- Explicit `ComponentNameProps` interface above the component.
- Discriminated unions over boolean flags + optional fields.
- `React.forwardRef` for DOM-wrapping primitives.

## Rendering & data
- Data-fetching extracted into `useComponentName` hook; component stays presentational.
- Always handle isLoading / isError / empty states explicitly.
- Subscribe to real-time via a hook; never instantiate WebSocket in a component.
- Lazy-load page-level components: `React.lazy` + `Suspense` + skeleton fallback.

## Performance
- `React.memo` / `useCallback` / `useMemo` only after profiling.
- Virtualise lists >100 items (`@tanstack/react-virtual`).

## Styling (vanilla-extract)
- Sibling `.css.ts` file; pull every value from `@app/design-tokens`.
- Themes via `createTheme` + `themeContract`. No JS-driven layout queries — use `@media`.

## Accessibility
- Semantic HTML first. Every interactive element keyboard-reachable.
- Modals trap focus; restore on close. Forms paired with `<label>`.
- Live regions for real-time updates: `aria-live="polite"` (or `"assertive"` for critical).

## Stories
- Every shared `packages/ui` component: default + variants + loading + error + empty states.
